        "id": 1002053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-11T20:14:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This field indicate in which state the sensor is powered up. Looking at the firecrest schematics, sensors are powered with 3D3V_SEN_S0, so they need to be reinitialize at every transition into S0.\n\nThe board layout may be wrong, I would expect the sensors to up in S3 to calculate lid angle while suspended. See below.",
      "parentUuid": "8cd86e55_41450c3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "fa9bce1674de02571996c264fa37fb213fb2b2bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71d60a82_3a42a91f",
        "filename": "board/arcada_ish/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1311094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T00:15:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we follow up with an EE about how the sensor is powered, if we need it to be on a different rail? That seems very time sensitive if so.",
      "parentUuid": "3512e5a7_bc0abe8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "fa9bce1674de02571996c264fa37fb213fb2b2bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "baf9b05f_b4c4606a",
        "filename": "board/arcada_ish/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T21:51:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The sensors (and ISH) are only going to be powered on during S0. The ISH is only providing the 180 degree signal. There are two other hall sensors that provide the lid open/closed signal to the EC which will wake up the AP.\n\n\nThe 180 degree signal is used for tablet mode detection and should be routed through the EC to the AP.\n\nOtherwise the raw sensor data from sensors is available to the OS and apps.",
      "parentUuid": "71d60a82_3a42a91f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "fa9bce1674de02571996c264fa37fb213fb2b2bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5536184e_26bd7efe",
        "filename": "board/arcada_ish/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1311094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-11T18:55:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this saying that in S0, the ISH will sample the sensor at a rate of 130 Hz. The sensor won\u0027t be sampled at all by the AP (this makes sense, as all data will go through the ISH, yes?) and the sensor won\u0027t be sampled by the ISH in S3 or S5. It would eventually need to get sampled in S3 to wake on a lid open, right? \n\nI don\u0027t understand what the ec_rate is setting here, the explanation in motion_sense.h isn\u0027t great. What is this setting? I also am nervous that you use MSEC, but the motion_sense.h says this value should be in units of uSec.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "fa9bce1674de02571996c264fa37fb213fb2b2bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9bd253a7_136f27c3",
        "filename": "board/arcada_ish/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-11T20:14:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "13Hz, not 130Hz. \nAll sensor data go through the EC.\nIt is not necessary yet, but will be once the lid accel is added to calculate the lid angle.\n\nLid open can be detected with the hall sensor.\nBut ultimately, the accelerometers should be sampled in S3 as well to prevent wake up on keyboard event when the user transition from clamshell to tablet while in S3.\n\nec_rate is the period the EC wakes up to retrieve accelerometer data to calculate lid angle. It will be removed once FIFO/Interrupt mode is supported by ISH.",
      "parentUuid": "5536184e_26bd7efe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "fa9bce1674de02571996c264fa37fb213fb2b2bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bf361833_7f22e00a",
        "filename": "board/arcada_ish/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1311094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T00:15:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oops on my bad Hz math. We don\u0027t need the sensors for ARC++ do we? Playing a game with a tilt sensor at 13Hz probably wouldn\u0027t be good.\nAck on sensor data going through EC.\nAck on FIFO/interrupt mode.\n\nAnyone else, do you know about our needs for the sensor in S3?",
      "parentUuid": "9bd253a7_136f27c3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "fa9bce1674de02571996c264fa37fb213fb2b2bd",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ab0d4f8_bcdb9f3f",
        "filename": "board/arcada_ish/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 58,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T21:51:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding the need for S3/S0ix lid angle calculations:\n - I think the device is actually suppose to wake up when it transitions clamshell -\u003e tablet or tablet -\u003e clamshell. The AP wakes up so it can set the correct wake sources again.\n - Without lid angle availability during S3, we can\u0027t wake up the AP to kick off the above process, which is definitely an issue.\n\nFor now, I want to leave S0 only config since that reflect the hardware.\n\nI am however trying to figure out what our options are going forward with getting lid angle in S0ix (b/120295222#comment25)",
      "parentUuid": "bf361833_7f22e00a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 58,
        "endChar": 4
      },
